<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ala al-Dawla Muhammad</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1041</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Ibn Kakuya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ala al-Dawla Muhammad, known as Ibn Kakuya, was the founder of the Kakuyid dynasty. Appointed governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isfahan">Isfahan</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buyid-dynasty">Buyids</a> around 1008, he made himself independent ruler of Isfahan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamadan">Hamadan</a>. The philosopher <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avicenna">Avicenna</a> served at his court as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vizier">vizier</a> and physician and wrote major works there. He was repeatedly pressed by the Ghaznavids.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ala-al-dawla-muhammad.jpg" alt="Ala al-Dawla Muhammad" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Classical Numismatic Group; [1] · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MuhammadibnRustamDushmanziyarCoin.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
